IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ncc-cadets`

-- National Cadet Corps Act 1972, ss 4(3), 8, 9(4), (5), 11 to 17 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_national-cadet-corps-act-1972.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`a defiant refusal of a lawful order` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `disobeyed a command` IS TRUE
    `the command was lawful` IS TRUE
    `the command was given or conveyed personally` IS TRUE
    `in a manner showing wilful defiance of authority` IS TRUE
    `contravened an order or regulation under the Act` IS FALSE
    `knew the order or regulation` IS FALSE
    `might reasonably be expected to know it` IS FALSE

`a sulky but not defiant disobedience` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `disobeyed a command` IS TRUE
    `the command was lawful` IS TRUE
    `the command was given or conveyed personally` IS TRUE
    `in a manner showing wilful defiance of authority` IS FALSE
    `contravened an order or regulation under the Act` IS FALSE
    `knew the order or regulation` IS FALSE
    `might reasonably be expected to know it` IS FALSE

`a defiant refusal of an unlawful order` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `disobeyed a command` IS TRUE
    `the command was lawful` IS FALSE
    `the command was given or conveyed personally` IS TRUE
    `in a manner showing wilful defiance of authority` IS TRUE
    `contravened an order or regulation under the Act` IS FALSE
    `knew the order or regulation` IS FALSE
    `might reasonably be expected to know it` IS FALSE

`a breach of a standing order the cadet knew` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `disobeyed a command` IS FALSE
    `the command was lawful` IS FALSE
    `the command was given or conveyed personally` IS FALSE
    `in a manner showing wilful defiance of authority` IS FALSE
    `contravened an order or regulation under the Act` IS TRUE
    `knew the order or regulation` IS TRUE
    `might reasonably be expected to know it` IS FALSE

`a breach of an order the cadet should have known` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `disobeyed a command` IS FALSE
    `the command was lawful` IS FALSE
    `the command was given or conveyed personally` IS FALSE
    `in a manner showing wilful defiance of authority` IS FALSE
    `contravened an order or regulation under the Act` IS TRUE
    `knew the order or regulation` IS FALSE
    `might reasonably be expected to know it` IS TRUE

`a cadet hurt on exercise by an on-duty officer, certified` MEANS Incident WITH
    `the harm is death or personal injury` IS TRUE
    `the injured person is a member` IS TRUE
    `the injured person was on duty` IS TRUE
    `the injured person was on Corps land, premises, ship, aircraft or vehicle` IS FALSE
    `the Minister certifies it attributable to service` IS TRUE
    `the wrongdoer is a member on duty` IS TRUE
    `the court is satisfied the act was unconnected with duty` IS FALSE
    `caused by the condition of Corps premises, equipment or supplies` IS FALSE
    `the wrongdoer is a Government officer` IS FALSE

